  "id": "34-in-conflict",
  "title": "A reused iseq with a different payload is E_IN_CONFLICT, never a silent dup",
  "spec": "5.4",
  "description": "The daemon records sha256(payload)[:16] with every final answer. A different payload under an iseq it already answered means the client's counter and the daemon's state disagree (lost outbox, cloned host); the daemon refuses with E_IN_CONFLICT (nothing consumed) and the client rotates `ie` for that link and sends the text as iseq 1 of the new key.",
